sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-honda-dichotomous-tree-branching> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-honda-dichotomous-tree-branching-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-honda-dichotomous-tree-branching-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Honda (1971) J. Theor. Biol. & Honda & Fisher (1978) Science 3D recursive dichotomous tree branching, effective leaf area optimization, Leonardo da Vinci pipe-model area conservation, and solar-elevation ray tracing of tiered crowns vs latitude — MorphoEval overall 91.2/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 3 (v3) evaluation of `1976-honda-dichotomous-tree-branching.py` (overall weighted score 91.2/100, down from 94.1/100 in v2). The single Pass 2 remediation item is closed in a reduced but honest form: a new section couples stacked Honda & Fisher tiers to Campbell & Norman (1998) solar geometry with Cooper (1969) declinations over 12 months x hourly hour angles, ray-traces tier-to-tier shadows with Monsi & Saeki Beer-Lambert attenuation, and sweeps 6 latitudes x 14 tier spacings to give a parameter-free 90% saturation spacing s_90/R = 1.832 at the equator vs 0.969 at 45 deg N and 0.850 at Meise (ratio 1.89 vs null 1.0), with the specimen's projected tier spacing s/R = 0.376 +- 0.134 capturing E = 0.747 at Meise vs 0.621 at the equator. Two new Lean 4 theorems (shadow-offset monotonicity, stacked Beer-Lambert optical depth) bring the total to 5 with 0 sorrys; measurements grew from 9 to 16 and self-test suites from 8 to 10 (all pass, 13 s). The score falls because this round examined the reference anchors v2 accepted: the Honda & Fisher \"benchmark\" curve (r = 0.9978) and the specimen references in the reference JSON are the script's own earlier outputs, three new measurements have no external reference, the CV junction filter pre-selects the Honda & Fisher angle window, and the 3D builder and the solar section use uncited constants. Overall 91.2/100 (faithfulness 90.3, reproducibility 93.3); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 028758bc; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 92, Morphological realism / specimen match 90, Parameter expressivity 91, Morphometric validation 88, Source and data traceability 93, Code-to-model traceability 94, Reproducibility package 93. Output judged: docs/media/dichotomous_tree_branching_comparison.png: rendered output of 1976-honda-dichotomous-tree-branching.py at 028758bc, image/png, 2148088 B, 2475×1575 px, artifact_sha256 581f4f616734e5fca1c57a025888323716a41e79137972f0611843524777aceb (sha256 581f4f616734e5fca1c57a025888323716a41e79137972f0611843524777aceb), spec_fingerprint 7cfa8b501a15c214e965ecf451b63af5fa8b3bb7f3a5e144483628cccc87fe3b. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 7cfa8b501a15c214e965ecf451b63af5fa8b3bb7f3a5e144483628cccc87fe3b; artifact_sha256: 581f4f616734e5fca1c57a025888323716a41e79137972f0611843524777aceb; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/dichotomous_tree_branching/cornus_controversa_tiered_crown_specimen.jpg=47cbd7225997789e..., datasets/dichotomous_tree_branching/dichotomous_tree_branching_reference.json=9b8cd89b9fa19fbf..., datasets/dichotomous_tree_branching/solar_tier_spacing_reference.json=640596fc8c3df302...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-dichotomous-tree-branching-audit-v2. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Honda (1971) J. Theor. Biol. 31(2):331-338 3D recursive vector-rotation tree architecture parameterized by daughter divergence angles (theta_1, theta_2), length contraction ratios (r_1, r_2), and vertical phyllotactic roll angle alpha = 137.5 deg in the local horizontal plane spanned by v and v x z_hat | Honda & Fisher (1978) Science 199(4331):888-890 & Fisher & Honda (1979) Am. J. Bot. 66:633-644 demonstration that empirical branching angles (theta_1 approx 24-32 deg, theta_2 approx 52-62 deg) and contraction ratios (r_1 = 0.90, r_2 = 0.70) in Terminalia catappa and Cornus controversa maximize non-overlapping effective leaf area A_eff / A_total across 5-branch horizontal whorls | Shinozaki et al. (1964) Jpn. J. Ecol. 14:97-105 pipe-model theory and Eloy (2011) Phys. Rev. Lett. 107:258101 wind-stress derivation of Leonardo da Vinci's cross-sectional area conservation d_parent^Delta = d_1^Delta + d_2^Delta (Delta = 2.0) | Campbell & Norman (1998) Ch. 11 solar geometry sin h = sin(phi) sin(delta) + cos(phi) cos(delta) cos(H) with Cooper (1969) declination delta = 23.45 sin(2 pi (284 + n)/365) and the Monsi & Saeki (1953) Beer-Lambert canopy extinction tau = exp(-LAI); reconstructed_in_script: Full Honda (1971) 3D rotation-matrix tree builder (`grow_honda_1971_3d_tree`) across 4 botanical crown archetypes (excurrent conifer, pagoda tiered Cornus, decurrent deliquescent Quercus, weeping pendulous Salix) over k = 6 orders (127 internodes, 64 terminal leaf clusters) | Honda & Fisher (1978) 5-whorl horizontal tier disk-union integration (`compute_effective_leaf_area_ratio`) and 2D (theta_1, theta_2) optimization surface (`evaluate_honda_fisher_optimization_surface`), Pearson r = 0.99782 against the vendored 8-regime benchmark curve, Terminalia (0.7739) and Cornus (0.7591) vs the collinear theta_1 = theta_2 = 0 ablation control (0.2001, 74.14% self-shading penalty) | Exact Leonardo da Vinci / Shinozaki pipe-model sapwood area conservation (sum d_{k,i}^2 / d_0^2 = 1.0000 across all 6 orders and 63 bifurcations) contrasted against Murray's cube law (Delta = 3.0) and untapered cylinder controls | Pass 3: diurnal/seasonal direct-beam sun paths at 6 latitudes (0, 15, 30, 45, 50.93 Meise, 60 deg N), a 7-tier stacked Honda & Fisher crown ray-traced tier-to-tier with Beer-Lambert tau_c^n attenuation (tau_c = exp(-2) = 0.135), annual beam light capture E(s/R) over 14 tier spacings, parameter-free 90% saturation spacing s_90/R = 1.832 (0 deg), 0.969 (45 deg), 0.850 (Meise), 0.710 (60 deg), ratio s_90(0)/s_90(45) = 1.89, and the specimen's projected tier spacing s/R = 0.376 +- 0.134 giving E = 0.747 at Meise vs 0.621 if transplanted to the equator | Computer-vision segmentation of the Pagoda Dogwood (Cornus controversa 'Variegata') specimen (`cornus_controversa_tiered_crown_specimen.jpg`, Botanic Garden Meise, 960x1280 px) detecting 7 horizontal pagoda foliage tiers, 25 Y-bifurcations with theta_1 = 22.40 +- 8.18 deg, theta_2 = 50.93 +- 14.23 deg, Leonardo area ratio 0.9533 +- 0.1705, and 6 inter-tier spacing pairs; transfer_boundary: 3D recursive vector-rotation internode skeletons and 2D horizontal whorl leaf-cluster disk unions mapped to optical crown stratigraphy and woody bifurcation geometry of Cornus controversa | The ray-traced 'tiered crown' is a stack of planar Honda & Fisher 5-whorl disk-union tiers with a uniform per-tier transmittance, not the 3D Honda (1971) internode skeleton of `grow_honda_1971_3d_tree`; light capture is direct beam only (no diffuse sky radiance, no leaf scattering, no penumbra), and the latitude prediction is validated against the null ratio 1.0 and self-consistency, not against measured tier spacings across latitudes | The Honda & Fisher benchmark curve, the specimen theta_1/theta_2/beta/tier references and the specimen s/R reference in the vendored JSON files are values previously produced by this script (regression anchors), not digitised figure values or independent measurements; does_not_claim: Cambial auxin-cytokinin molecular transport kinetics, turbulent eddy-resolvable wind-tunnel aeroelasticity at individual leaf blades, diffuse-sky or scattered-light radiative transfer, photosynthetic light-response curves, or a literature-anchored optimal tier spacing vs latitude." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: 1976-honda-dichotomous-tree-branching.py:1113-1149 and 1198-1218 — measurements 10, 11 and 16 carry `reference_value: None` and measurement 14 (1174-1186) uses the equator transplant as its reference. Add at least one external anchor for tier spacing (e.g. digitised internode/tier spacing of Terminalia catappa from Fisher & Honda 1979 or Cornus controversa herbarium/forestry measurements) or a published canopy light- interception value for a pagoda crown, and move the anchor-less items to a `predictions` list.",
            "remediation needed: 1976-honda-dichotomous-tree-branching.py:1507 and 1742-1838 — the growth GIF is unchanged Pass 2 content and the self-test runs the full latitude sweep twice (13 s). Add the tier-spacing / shadow mechanism to the primary GIF (or cross-link the solar GIF from the comparison figure) and cache the sweep between the two determinism calls.",
            "remediation needed: 1976-honda-dichotomous-tree-branching.py:1845-1852 and 1864-1868 — `--theta1/--theta2/--r1/--r2/--orders/ --tiers/--tau-cluster/--latitudes` affect only rendering; `measure_morphoeval()` (971) hard-codes the defaults and `--latitudes` silently appends Meise. Thread the parsed arguments into `measure_morphoeval()` and make the Meise append explicit (warn or require).",
            "remediation needed: 1976-honda-dichotomous-tree-branching.py:221-222, 239, 586, 1215 — pitch factors 0.25*t1 / -0.18*t2, the daughter-2 pi/2 roll, the tier-order schedule max(2, 5 - 4t//n) and LAI_c = 2 are uncited. Either cite a source (Honda 1971 Fig. 4 for pitch; Fisher & Honda 1979 for tier order; a Cornus LAI measurement) or expose them as documented free parameters in the docstring and the math-KG YAML.",
            "remediation needed: 1976-honda-dichotomous-tree-branching.py:643-692 and 566-610 — the ray tracer consumes stacked planar Honda & Fisher disk-union tiers with a uniform tau_c, not the 3D Honda internode skeleton of `grow_honda_1971_3d_tree` (150-261). Rasterise the 3D skeleton's terminal leaf clusters per height band so the ray-traced crown is the Honda (1971) tree, and add a diffuse-sky (UOC or SOC) term beside the direct beam.",
            "remediation needed: 1976-honda-dichotomous-tree-branching.py:933-935, 843, 850, 871 — junction acceptance windows 12-50 / 30-82 deg and beta in [0.65, 1.45], the ROI box and the 72nd / 78th percentile thresholds pre-select Y-forks inside the expected Honda & Fisher range. Report the unfiltered fork-angle distribution alongside the filtered one and run a threshold-sensitivity sweep so theta_1/theta_2/beta are measured, not prescribed.",
            "remediation needed: datasets/dichotomous_tree_branching/dichotomous_tree_branching_reference.json:46-103 with 1976-honda-dichotomous-tree-branching.py:404-470 and 1011-1047 — the `honda_fisher_1978_angle_sweep_benchmarks` values (0.2001, 0.7591, 0.7739, ...) are the script's own outputs, so Pearson r = 0.9978, the 0.7739 Terminalia reference and the 74.14% penalty reference are self-referential. Digitise the Honda & Fisher (1978) Fig. 2 / Fisher & Honda (1979) Table 1 effective-leaf-area values into a separately provenanced block and compute r against those; relabel the current block as a regression fixture.",
            "remediation needed: datasets/dichotomous_tree_branching/solar_citations_pass3.bib and 1976-honda-dichotomous-tree-branching.py:91-100 — the Pass 3 BibTeX file is not SHA-256-pinned and the pinning is split across `EXPECTED_SHA256` and `EXPECTED_SHA256_PASS3`. Merge the bib entries into a single pinned citations file (re-pin) and collapse the two checksum tables; verify the three new DOIs online when network is available." ;
        pk:hasScore "0.912"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Claude Fable 5.1 (MorphoEval Autonomous Loop Slot 051 Pass 3 Assessor)" ;
        dct:identifier "claude-fable-5-1" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> ;
        foaf:homepage <https://www.anthropic.com> .
}

